WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Does needing reassurance mean lacking independence?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Support and exploration can work together.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Attachment research studies closeness, response and exploration.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
A secure base describes a supportive relationship.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Age and research context remain important.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
A traveler can leave while knowing how to connect.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Reliable response can support exploration.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Approach for support, then explore when ready.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
The signal station is a teaching metaphor.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
One clingy moment cannot define attachment.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
One separation cannot judge a whole family.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Relationships can change with experience and context.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Agree on contact times and trusted people.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Name the kind of help you need.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Support can come from several reliable relationships.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Needing support need not bring shame.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Connection can coexist with your own path.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Know where the light is, then venture outward.
